{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Editor Setup Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Install VS Code"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "VS Code is the recommended editor. It is free, runs on every OS, has first-class Jupyter notebook support, and the extension ecosystem covers everything you need for AI work."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Download it from [code.visualstudio.com](https://code.visualstudio.com/)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Verify from the terminal:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "code --version"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "If `code` is not found on macOS, open VS Code, press `Cmd+Shift+P`, type \"Shell Command\", and select \"Install 'code' command in PATH\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Install Essential Extensions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Open the integrated terminal in VS Code (`Ctrl+`` ` or `` Cmd+` ``) and install the extensions that matter for AI work:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "code --install-extension ms-python.python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "code --install-extension ms-python.vscode-pylance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "code --install-extension ms-toolsai.jupyter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "code --install-extension eamodio.gitlens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "code --install-extension ms-vscode-remote.remote-ssh"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "code --install-extension ms-python.debugpy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "code --install-extension ms-python.black-formatter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "code --install-extension charliermarsh.ruff"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "What each one does:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Extension | Why |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "|-----------|-----|"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Python | Language support, virtual env detection, run/debug |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Pylance | Fast type checking, autocomplete, import resolution |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Jupyter | Run notebooks inside VS Code, variable explorer |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| GitLens | See who changed what, inline git blame |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Remote SSH | Open a folder on a remote GPU box as if it were local |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Debugpy | Step-through debugging for Python |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Black Formatter | Auto-format on save, consistent style |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Ruff | Fast linting, catches common mistakes |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The file `code/.vscode/extensions.json` in this lesson contains the full recommendations list. When you open the project folder, VS Code will prompt you to install them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Configure Settings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Copy the settings from `code/.vscode/settings.json` in this lesson, or apply them manually through `Settings > Open Settings (JSON)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The key settings for AI work:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```jsonc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "{"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"python.analysis.typeCheckingMode\": \"basic\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"editor.formatOnSave\": true,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"editor.rulers\": [88, 120],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"notebook.output.scrolling\": true,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"files.autoSave\": \"afterDelay\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Why these matter:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Type checking on basic**: Catches wrong argument types before you run. Saves debugging time on tensor shape mismatches and wrong API parameters."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Format on save**: Never think about formatting again. Black handles it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Rulers at 88 and 120**: Black wraps at 88. The 120 marker shows when docstrings and comments are getting too long."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Notebook output scrolling**: Training loops print thousands of lines. Without scrolling, the output panel explodes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Auto-save**: You will forget to save. Your training script will run stale code. Auto-save prevents that."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Terminal Integration"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "VS Code's integrated terminal is where you run training scripts, monitor GPUs, and manage environments."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Set it up properly:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```jsonc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "{"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"terminal.integrated.defaultProfile.osx\": \"zsh\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"terminal.integrated.defaultProfile.linux\": \"bash\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"terminal.integrated.fontSize\": 13,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"terminal.integrated.scrollback\": 10000"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Useful shortcuts:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Action | macOS | Linux/Windows |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "|--------|-------|---------------|"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Toggle terminal | `` Ctrl+` `` | `` Ctrl+` `` |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| New terminal | `Ctrl+Shift+`` ` | `Ctrl+Shift+`` ` |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Split terminal | `Cmd+\\` | `Ctrl+\\` |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Split terminals are useful: one for running your script, one for monitoring GPU with `nvidia-smi -l 1` or `watch -n 1 nvidia-smi`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Remote Development (SSH into GPU Boxes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This is the most important extension for AI work. You will run training on remote machines (cloud VMs, lab servers, Lambda, Vast.ai). Remote SSH lets you open the remote filesystem, edit files, run terminals, and debug as if everything were local."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Setup:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1. Install the Remote SSH extension (done in Step 2)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "2. Press `Ctrl+Shift+P` (or `Cmd+Shift+P`), type \"Remote-SSH: Connect to Host\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "3. Enter `user@your-gpu-box-ip`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "4. VS Code installs its server component on the remote machine automatically."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For passwordless access, set up SSH keys:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C \"your-email@example.com\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ssh-copy-id user@your-gpu-box-ip"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Add the host to `~/.ssh/config` for convenience:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Host gpu-box"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    HostName 203.0.113.50"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    User ubuntu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ForwardAgent yes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Now `Remote-SSH: Connect to Host > gpu-box` connects instantly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Install VS Code and all extensions listed in Step 2\n2. Copy the `settings.json` from this lesson into your VS Code config\n3. Open a Python file and verify that Pylance shows type hints and Black formats on save\n4. If you have access to a remote machine, set up Remote SSH and open a folder on it"
      ]
    }
